// Where this project's signing settings come from, and why they are not here.
//
// The .xcodeproj is generated (`xcodegen generate`) and ignored by git, so a
// development team set in Xcode's own Signing & Capabilities tab lives exactly
// until the next generation — which happens after every added source file, and
// several times a day when more than one session is working. The symptom is
// Xcode asking for the team again before a device build, over and over, as if
// it had forgotten. It had not; the file it wrote to had been replaced.
//
// The team is written here instead, through a file that is NOT in the
// repository: the Apple account behind it was deliberately taken out of HEAD
// on 10 Sep 2026 and does not come back through a build setting. `#include?`
// is the optional include — a clone or a CI checkout without the local file
// generates and builds exactly as before, with no team and no error, which is
// what every simulator build and the whole of `verify.sh` needs.
//
// To create it, once, from the certificate already in your keychain:
//
//   security find-identity -v -p codesigning \
//     | sed -n 's/.*(\([A-Z0-9]\{10\}\))"$/\1/p' | head -1 \
//     | sed 's/^/DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = /' > ios/Signing.local.xcconfig
//
// See docs/SETUP.md.
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
